{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/17831-mortals-with-prolonged-exposure-to-the-hedge","id":17831,"title":"Mortals with prolonged exposure to the Hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-25T11:39:38-08:00","id":17831,"title":"Mortals with prolonged exposure to the Hedge","content":"So a question came up that I'm curious about. Let say a mortal has had extended exposure to the Hedge via repeated Hedge Diving / Journeying with Changelings (but never went to arcadia). I know that the Thorns tear at the soul. Does mortal undergo any physical changes do to the exposure? Does he gain something akin Enscrollment or Fae-touched? Does the person learn some sort of hedge wizard magic ala Second Sight associated with Changeling abilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T11:55:13-08:00","id":17839,"title":"","content":"Some of that is mentioned in passing in Autumn Nightmares. Long-term residence in the Hedge and living off of goblin fruits turns humans into inhuman wretches, broken in both mind and body. Presumably they turn into some form of hobgoblin, and the book claims that staying in the Hedge for several months is enough to ruin even those kindly treated. Lesser exposure, who knows? It's pretty solely in homebrewing territory for the immediate future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T14:04:12-08:00","id":17918,"title":"","content":"Its assumed mortals will degenerate into some sort of hob goblin eventually. Many of the Hobgoblin species like Briar Wolves are rumored to originate from mortals lost in the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T15:06:22-08:00","id":17955,"title":"","content":"It's Arcadia where humans get the real nifty changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T11:38:30-08:00","id":18557,"title":"","content":"Thanks for info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T17:10:42-08:00","id":21984,"title":"","content":"I actually had an idea for a lab experiment where goldfish and guppies get kept in the hedge. Maybe some plants too. <br /> Now would be a horrible time for my character to do that though because our current campaign has the Iron Shield, a group of changelings ready and eager to kill anyone suspected of being too close to the fae.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1477-randompaul","name":"Randompaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T16:38:20-08:00","id":22711,"title":"","content":"Does being ensorcelled help, do you think? I'm guessing that the &quot;become a wretch after months worth of exposure&quot; would cover staying in hollows or is that through exposure to the thorns? Hollows, themselves, are relatively safe (though sanity draining over time, I'm sure) so I'm wondering how the physical changes would manifest and how long it would take.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T22:49:04-08:00","id":22951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Randompaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/17831-mortals-with-prolonged-exposure-to-the-hedge?p=21984#post21984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually had an idea for a lab experiment where goldfish and guppies get kept in the hedge. Maybe some plants too.<br /> Now would be a horrible time for my character to do that though because our current campaign has the Iron Shield, a group of changelings ready and eager to kill anyone suspected of being too close to the fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a degenerating act to clarity. It rings too strongly of how Fae kidnap and warp their &quot;Pets&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T19:35:51-08:00","id":23455,"title":"","content":"Would that apply to plant experiments too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1477-randompaul","name":"Randompaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T20:14:44-08:00","id":23475,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think so, but I imagine some more anti-Fae NPCs might. Bridgeburners and such. Alternatively the intrusion could get the attention of hobs and the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T22:09:27-08:00","id":23538,"title":"","content":"At this rate I'll never get to turn Finn into a gentleman-scientist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1477-randompaul","name":"Randompaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T13:21:20-08:00","id":23929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/17831-mortals-with-prolonged-exposure-to-the-hedge?p=22951#post22951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a degenerating act to clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>/:-/ Really? What level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T13:49:11-08:00","id":23952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/17831-mortals-with-prolonged-exposure-to-the-hedge?p=23929#post23929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">/:-/ Really? What level?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Carrying a mortal animal into the Hedge and leaving the animal there counts as a breaking point for changelings of Clarity 3 and higher (rolling two dice to avoid degeneration) \u2014 the changeling is deliberately attempting to alter a living being for her own purposes, in what is certainly a cruel fashion. The similarities to the Others\u2019 practice of kidnapping and altering \u201clower forms of life\u201d are impossible to ignore, even if she tries to rationalize them away.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}